Method-level choices (builder's call per ODD §1.1):

  - Symlink target = directory, not file. Anthropic discovery is
    per-directory (`<workspace>/.claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`),
    and skills can ship companion files; whole-directory
    symlinking preserves the discovery walk's view.
  - Walk only directory-shape skills (containing SKILL.md);
    flat-file `<plugin>/skills/<name>.md` shapes (e.g.,
    dev-sdlc/skills/start-project.md) are silently skipped.
  - Cross-plugin collision detection: alphabetical sort order
    means the first plugin wins; second raises. The early-return
    does NOT roll back already-symlinked first-plugin skills —
    this is acceptable because the operator's resolution (rename
    one of the colliding plugin skills) will converge to a clean
    state on the next scaffold run.
  - `PluginSkillCollisionError` uses ERR_HANDS_OFF_INTERNAL
    (-32099) error code, matching the existing scaffold-internal
    error code convention per first_run_scaffold.py:75 +
    `PluginAgentCollisionError`.
  - Reuses `_resolve_plugins_root` from Cycle 1 — same canonical/
    derived layout logic. No code duplication.
  - Tests = 4 NEW files: AC.LAYERED.2 (9 tests), AC.LAYERED.3+4
    (8 tests), AC.LAYERED.5 (8 tests), AC.LAYERED.7 (3 tests).
    27 new tests; all pass.
  - Wired into `run_first_run_scaffold` immediately after the
    Cycle 1 `_symlink_plugin_agents(Path(ws))` call; same
    `written.extend(...)` pattern. Plugin-skill writes appear in
    the scaffold's `files_written` tuple.
  - The .gitkeep helper (`_write_skills_gitkeep`) and the
    symlink helper (`_symlink_plugin_skills`) are order-
    independent: the symlink helper creates the skills dir
    if missing (robustness).

